  "analysis": "Both responses outline a multi‑lane plan, feature‑flag gating, and required security/VP approvals. JZW goes further by naming the release‑candidate branch, proposing a concrete split of unit vs. full regression tests to cut the 45‑minute CI window, defining a 4‑hour soak test to tame the flaky mock IdP, and spelling out precise rollback steps (code revert, flag toggle, cookie safety). LXD is less specific on CI optimisation and the IdP stability work, and its lane descriptions are more generic. Consequently JZW provides a clearer, more actionable roadmap with fewer likely follow‑up questions.",
